<title>GERMANY: AM Leben plans rights issue, steady dividend.</title>
<headline>AM Leben plans rights issue, steady dividend.</headline>
<dateline>AACHEN, Germany 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German life insurer Aachener und Muenchener Lebensversicherung AG said on Wednesday it planned to raise its nominal share capital by eight million marks to 88 million marks in a one-for-10 rights offering, with new shares priced at 100 marks.</p>
<p>The new shares will be entitled to dividend from January 1, 1997. The proposed capital raising will be submitted for approval to the annual shareholders' meeting on May 5, the company said in a mandatory statement.</p>
<p>Aachener und Muenchener also said it planned to pay an unchanged dividend of 12.50 marks on 1996 results.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
